# Bump this integer ONLY when the DCF output (fair_value / MoS / verdict /
# score) for an EXISTING ticker would change vs the prior version. That is
# the single trigger. Every other change -- observability, new endpoints,
# error sanitization, logging, metadata, frontend wiring, schema additions
# that don't touch analysis output -- must NOT bump this.
# (This edit is a no-op trigger to force a Railway redeploy that kills a
# runaway background job. Not a semantic change.)
#
# Why the discipline matters: a bump invalidates every cached analysis in
# Railway memory. Users hitting the site during that window see 10-30s
# response times (yfinance fallback on uncached tickers) instead of the
# normal ~200ms. Today we bumped this 21 times in 12 hours and caused
# real latency problems. Don't do that again.
#
# Decision checklist before bumping:
#   - Would TCS / INFY / any existing top-100 ticker's fair_value change?
#     YES  -> bump required
#     NO   -> continue to the next question.
#   - Would red_flags_structured / strengths change for any ticker?
#     (New W-rule or I-rule added, severity threshold moved, allowlist
#     extended, etc.)
#     YES  -> bump required. Cached payloads predating the rule would
#             serve empty red_flags / strengths for affected tickers —
#             the UI then shows "Red Flags: None" and "No strengths
#             found" on stocks that should fire new rules.
#     NO   -> do not bump, even if you changed analysis_service.py
CACHE_VERSION = 135  # 135: day92-utility-bear-floor (2026-05-22). Audit #4 (2026-05-22) found NTPC.NS + POWERGRID.NS shipping bear_case=0.0 / mos=+0.0% on the public stock-summary endpoint — the regulated-utility valuation engine (regulated_utility_valuation_service.compute_regulated_utility_fair_value) does produce sensible bear/bull (0.75/1.25 * base = Gordon ± tariff true-up band) but the analysis pipeline rebuilt _sc_bear_pre / _sc_bull_pre from scenarios_raw (DCF cash flows) for the non-financial branch. Regulated utilities short-circuit DCF, so scenarios_raw is empty and bear collapsed to 0. _enforce_scenario_order then accepted (0 <= base <= bull) as ordered. Fix: extend the financial-branch direct-from-bear_iv pathway to also fire for regulated_utility engines (is_regulated_utility_ticker AND _regulated_val_result.fair_value > 0), with a Day-56-style defensive floor (bear >= min(0.85*price, iv*0.95), bull >= max(1.10*price, iv*1.05)) so the bear case never collapses again even if the engine output is overwritten downstream. Affected tickers (universe scan): NTPC, POWERGRID, NLCINDIA, JSWENERGY, NTPCGREEN, IREDA, and any other ticker in REGULATED_UTILITY_TICKERS that currently surfaces bear_case=0. Bear/bull cases for these tickers will change materially (NTPC: 0/533/640 -> ~330/533/560; POWERGRID: 0/363/436 -> ~255/363/396). Base_case / fair_value / mos / verdict unchanged. feat/day84-pharma-quality-cohort (2026-05-22). Audit 2026-05-20 observed MANKIND FV Rs1,046 vs CMP Rs2,584 (-59.5%) — Day-53 widened canary bounds but the underlying engine still undershoots premium-quality Indian pharma franchises. Day-84 introduces a _PHARMA_FRANCHISE_TICKERS cohort (MANKIND / SUNPHARMA / CIPLA / TORNTPHARM / DRREDDY / DIVISLAB / ABBOTINDIA / GLAND / GLAXO / PFIZER / SANOFI / AJANTPHARM / ERIS) sitting between the hospital-chain and CDMO sub-buckets in the existing pharma engine hierarchy. Two coordinated levers: (1) WACC ceiling at 0.095 (same as hospitals — quasi-FMCG pricing power on domestic-OTC + branded chronic-care; bites on live measured WACC for every entry in the set, e.g. MANKIND 0.098 -> 0.095, DRREDDY 0.105 -> 0.095); (2) terminal-g floor lifted to 0.055 (same as hospital chains — India healthcare nominal-spend CAGR 12-15 percent per IRDAI / Ayushman Bharat / demographic aging; one notch below FMCG brand-moat tail TITAN 0.06). Two-block implementation mirrors Day-21 architecture: forecaster-side block (orphaned, kept in sync for diagnostics) + service-side SSOT in the terminal_g finalisation block before DCFEngine. WACC cap order is hospital -> franchise -> CDMO so DIVISLAB (in both franchise and CDMO sets) picks up the tighter franchise treatment. Terminal-g cap order is identical for the same reason. Cache bump required because the FV / MoS / verdict / score for all 13 franchise tickers materially changes (rough math: MANKIND TV multiple lifts ~20 percent from spread 0.048 -> 0.040, FV Rs1,046 -> ~Rs1,250-1,400, still below design-doc target Rs1,500-1,800 but a real step in the right direction; SUNPHARMA / CIPLA / DRREDDY / ABBOTINDIA similar 15-25 percent FV lift). Generic-pharma exporters (AUROPHARMA / ZYDUSLIFE / GLENMARK / IPCALAB / LAURUSLABS / etc.) keep the existing 0.105 WACC floor + 0.035 TG cap — US-pricing-pressure risk premium is unchanged. CDMO sub-bucket (SYNGENE / COHANCE / ANTHEM / SAGILITY / IKS) unchanged at 0.105 WACC cap + 0.045 TG lift. MANKIND's existing terminal_growth_override=0.05 + skip_ipo_routing=True remain in place; the new franchise lift sits on TOP of the override (lift kicks in when terminal_g less than 0.055, so the override at 0.05 gets re-raised to 0.055). # # # # 133: 133: fix/day76-reverse-dcf-cyclical-fix (2026-05-22). Reverse-DCF audit 2026-05-20 P5: RELIANCE surfacing "Market is pricing in 50% growth" (=SEARCH_MAX_GROWTH peg; refining-cycle FCF trough) and HDFCBANK "-5% growth" (=SEARCH_MIN_GROWTH peg; post-HDFC-merger balance-sheet inflation). Three fixes layered: (1) bank-skip gate at /api/v1/public/reverse-dcf/{ticker} via is_bank_like — returns structured {applicable: False, reason, category: "bank_like"} payload with header X-Cache: MISS-NOT-APPLICABLE so the frontend can render "see ROE/RoA panel instead" instead of hiding; (2) router-level cyclical fallback that synthesizes normalized_fcf := current_revenue × fcf_margin_5y when QualityOutput.normalized_fcf_cr is null on legacy/pre-v131 cached payloads — closes the gap on RELIANCE-class cyclicals where the upstream stash from forecaster._compute_fcf_base never made it to the router for tickers analysed under v130 or earlier; (3) service-level boundary-peg telemetry: when the bisector pegs at SEARCH_MIN_GROWTH / SEARCH_MAX_GROWTH without convergence, growth_off_scale=True is added to the response and the plain-English summary becomes ">= X.X% / <= X.X%" with a "trailing-margin anchor likely distorted by cyclical trough or balance-sheet event" caveat instead of a spurious precise number. Cache bump required because the reverse_dcf_v1 payload shape gains three new keys (growth_off_scale, growth_pegged_high, growth_pegged_low) and the bank-skip path materially changes the response body for ~17 financial-services tickers in the canary universe. # # # # 132: fix/day74-audit-spot-fixes (2026-05-21). FIX-RELIANCE-PAYOUT-ZERO: Reliance audit 2026-05-20 flagged "Payout 0%" despite Rs 5.50/share dividend. Root cause: standalone /api/v1/analysis/{ticker}/dividends route calls DividendService with enriched=None, so the 2026-05-18 FIX-DIVIDEND-PAYOUT-ZERO recovery block (which needs enriched.latest_pat + enriched.shares) was skipped. _build_from_series now falls back to yfinance .info.trailingEps when enriched is absent --- same trailingEps recovery the non-DB-first path uses at lines ~120-133. Affects every ticker that paid TTM dividends but has yfinance .info.payoutRatio == null AND was hit via the standalone dividends route (Reliance confirmed; likely also TCS, INFY, HDFCBANK, ITC, HUL on that route). Day-74 daily-insight rotation does NOT touch cache (frontend only). # # # 131: fix/day73-post-demerger-routing (2026-05-21). Bug D: ITCHOTELS (Jan-2025 demerger) and ABLBL (recent demerger) were returning FV=0 / verdict="fairly_valued" / revenue_cagr_3y=null because generic DCF cannot stitch pre/post-demerger bases. Detect-and-route: when has_structural_break(ticker) is True AND quarters_since_event(ticker) < 8 (~<2y post-event), route through the IPO framework compute_sector_relative_fv peer-multiple path; tag valuation_engine_used = "relative_post_demerger"; validators.py skips the DCF-calibrated fair_value_ratio / margin_of_safety bounds + PHANTOM_REVENUE_CAGR (Rule 7) on this engine label. Sector-scope: * (any non-financial / non-utility / non-REIT / non-ETF ticker with a recent structural break). Cache bump required because the FV output for affected tickers changes from 0 to a positive peer-multiple FV --- frontend verdict + MoS rendering depends on it. # # # 130: fix/day66-moat-rendering-consistency (2026-05-21). Audit 2026-05-20 caught Reliance's analysis page rendering Moat card "Moderate" while the Strengths card listed "Wide Economic Moat" --- contradiction on one screen. Root cause: the Wide Moat strength fired at `m_score > 65 OR m_grade == "Wide"`, but the moat label threshold (screener/moat_engine.py:_MOAT_BAND_WIDE) is >=70. Scores 66-69 lit up the strength as Wide while the label said Moderate. Fix: align strength to grade only ("Wide" label is now the single source of truth for the Wide Moat strength). Affects any cached payload where score is in the 66-69 band --- previously emitted the conflicting strength, now will not. # # # 129: fix/day64-audit-polish-batch (2026-05-21). Audit 2026-05-20 low-hanging batch: PARADEEP / RCF / GNFC / GSFC / NFL / CHAMBLFERT / FACT / ZUARI / DEEPAKFERT / MADRASFERT pinned to "Chemicals" sector (was "General/Diversified" — broke peer-cohort + sector facet routing). Frontend changes (humanise local_db_parquet dev-string in footer, expand UNDER_REVIEW_VERDICTS for page-title to include under_review + low_confidence statuses) are render-only and don't affect cache. Sector-pin is engine-input though, so any prior cached payload for these 10 tickers must recompute to pick up the right sector classification. # # # 128: fix/day58-price-sanity-gates (2026-05-21). Defensive gates on canonical_price catch the TCS-class price-freeze bug (daily_prices stuck for months) and the INFY-class outlier bug (92x unit error / FX-conversion bug / wrong-ticker resolution). Two new helpers: _is_daily_prices_stale (rejects daily_prices rows older than 7 trading days) + _is_price_outlier (rejects any served price >40% off the 30-day daily_prices median). Both fail OPEN on insufficient history so new listings aren't false-rejected. Affected: any ticker whose live_quotes/daily_prices feed is broken or carrying a stale/anomalous value. TCS specifically: served ₹2,327 (Nov-2025 freeze) vs market ~₹3,500. After this PR, TCS will return None from the cascade → upstream renders 'data_limited' instead of a confidently-wrong price. # # # 127: fix/day56-bear-floor-respect-ordering (2026-05-21). Closes the third (and likely final) variant of the cyclical scenario-inversion family. After Day-51 (Tier-2 path) and Day-53c (generalized at use site), canary 2026-05-21 still showed HINDZINC/COROMANDEL/GUJGASLTD with bear > base — but coming from the SECONDARY bear-floor guard at service.py L3144+, not the trough-anchor path. That guard intentionally allowed bear >= base ("preferable to ₹1.59 display"). Fix: change `bear = 0.5 * price` to `bear = min(0.5 * price, 0.95 * iv)` so bear always lands strictly below base while staying well above the ₹0 pathology. For HINDZINC: bear 315 -> 291.7 (vs base 307). For IOC: bear 65.9 -> 46.9 (vs base 49.36, still well above the bare-engine ₹1.59). # # # 126: fix/day53c-trough-reclamp-at-use-site (2026-05-21). Generalizes the Day-51 re-clamp. The Day-51 fix only handled the Tier-2 cohort override path, but other override paths (growth-stock override on L2129+, any future override) can also reset iv after the trough anchor fired. Canary 2026-05-21 still failed on GUJGASLTD/HINDZINC/COROMANDEL via these paths. Fix: move the re-clamp to the point of USE in the scenario block (L3087+) where iv is final, so it's universal regardless of which earlier override path touched iv. Affects scenario bear/bull rendering for cyclicals at trough whose base iv lands below the trough-anchor's 0.85*price floor. # # # 125: fix/day51-cyclical-trough-tier2-reclamp (2026-05-20). Canary gate-3 fix. When trough_anchor fires (raw DCF iv < 0.2*price for a cyclical) AND Tier-2 cohort then overrides iv to the cohort FV, the previously-set _trough_anchor_bear_iv (0.85 * price) could exceed the new base iv, producing bear > base on metals/cement/gas (HINDALCO/HINDZINC/COROMANDEL/GUJGASLTD). Fix in service.py L2098+: re-clamp bear = min(0.85*price, iv*0.95) and bull = max(1.10*price, iv*1.05) so the band always brackets the new base. Affects ~4 known tickers + any future cyclical that lands in trough-anchor + Tier-2 path simultaneously. # # # 124: fix/day21-tg-lift-propagation (2026-05-20). Bug B fix. The Day-16/Day-19 terminal-g lift blocks inside FCFForecaster.predict() were structurally orphaned: they mutated a LOCAL _g_terminal_eff variable that never propagated to DCFEngine(terminal_growth=...) at service.py:1898. So the lift had ZERO effect on TV math despite the code paths existing — verified by absence of _hospital_chain_terminal_g_lifted and _pharma_cdmo_terminal_g_lifted flags across all 13 live payloads at cache_version=122. Moved the lift to service.py:~L1294 (immediately after the ticker_overrides terminal_g_override block and BEFORE DCFEngine construction). Mirrors the canonical sets in models/forecaster.py (test_tg_lift_set_membership_matches_forecaster locks in the parity). Hospitals: TG 0.040 -> 0.055. CDMOs: TG 0.040 -> 0.045. Combined with Day-20 WACC ceiling (hospitals capped at 0.095, CDMOs at 0.105), the wacc-g spread tightens to 0.040 / 0.060 respectively — both above the 0.020 Gordon-model safety floor. Expected: now-LIVE TG lift adds another +20-40% on top of the Day-20 WACC ceiling's +5-17% — bringing hospital FVs from current 0.16-0.64x consensus toward 0.40-0.85x. Sector-scope: pharma (same as Day-16/19).  # # # 123: fix/day20-part2-delhivery-override-retune (2026-05-20). DELHIVERY's Day-18 story-DCF override params (22% growth / 8% op margin / 70% reinvestment / 13.5% WACC) produced NEGATIVE enterprise value at the synthetic anchors — FCFFs stayed negative through year 7 and the PV of explicit period (-₹612 Cr) overwhelmed PV of TV (+₹292 Cr). Story-DCF returned None at the EV<=0 guard, so the Day-20 PR-#410 revenue-field fix had no observable effect for DELHIVERY — the rescue chain returned None and the safety-net logged the data_limited caveat. Retuned to v3: 22% growth / 15% target op margin (mature 3PL benchmark; BlueDart pre-COVID 14-16%) / 40% reinvestment (asset-light pivot priced) / 3y margin convergence / 12.5% WACC. With these params FV computes ₹205 vs CMP ₹459 (0.45x — comfortably inside [0.30, 3.50] safety-net band). FV still well below 22-analyst consensus ₹528 because this is a narrative model with conservative assumptions (confidence cap = 50 = 'story, not fact'). To match consensus would require terminal margin 18-20% which is a growth-investor scenario this engine intentionally does not model. Sector-scope: Internet Platform (single-ticker override). Expected post-recompute: DELHIVERY FV ₹64 -> ₹205, engine string flips to story_dcf_after_dcf_collapse, StoryDcfBadge fires on the frontend, confidence_score = 43-50.  # # # 122: fix/day20-wacc-ceiling-and-safety-net-revenue (2026-05-20). POST-validation fix. The impact_check_day14_19.py forced-warm + measurement showed only 3/24 named Day-14-19 tickers actually moved FV at cache_version=121 — 13/24 recomputed but produced near-same FV. Two root causes diagnosed via live payload inspection: (a) Day-16/Day-19 WACC FLOORS were no-ops because CAPM-derived hospital/CDMO WACCs sit at 0.098-0.128, already above the 0.085/0.095 floors. max(wacc_floor, X) returns unchanged CAPM. Switched to a POST-clip CEILING: hospitals capped at 0.095, CDMOs at 0.105 — these actually bite (e.g. AGARWALEYE 0.128 -> 0.095, ANTHEM/SAGILITY/IKS 0.128 -> 0.105). (b) Day-18 logistics rescue couldn't fire because the safety-net's _fin_sn dict at service.py:2574 was missing the 'revenue' field. compute_story_dcf_fair_value returns None at rev0<=0 guard, so DELHIVERY / PAYTM / MEESHO / ZOMATO / POLICYBZR / NYKAA / SWIGGY all failed the 3rd rescue rung — verified live for DELHIVERY (data_issues confirmed safety net fired but all 3 rungs returned None). Added 'revenue' + 'latest_revenue' to the dict. Expected post-recompute: hospitals FV move +30-50% (TV uplift from tighter wacc-g spread); CDMOs +20-40%; DELHIVERY now rescues via story-DCF (engine string flips to story_dcf_after_dcf_collapse). Defers Day-16/Day-19 terminal-g lift gating bug (TG flag absent from all payloads — needs more diagnosis) and ITCHOTELS/ABLBL no-cache-row bug (pipeline short-circuit on NULL eps_basic — separate PR). Sector-scope: pharma + Internet Platform (multi-sector — same scope as Day-16/Day-18/19).  # # # 121: feat/day18-19-logistics-cdmo (2026-05-20). Tier-2 outlier reduction PR #3 (after Day-16 hospital + Day-17 recent-IPO routing). TWO additive engine changes: (a) Day-18 logistics platforms (DELHIVERY/MAHLOG/ALLCARGO) added to TICKER_SECTOR_OVERRIDES->Internet Platform, routing them through the existing Story-DCF rescue rung when generic DCF collapses. DELHIVERY also gets a per-ticker override in config/story_dcf_overrides.json (initial_growth=0.22, target_op_margin=0.08, reinvestment_rate=0.70, wacc=0.135) calibrated to actual analyst guidance. Live scan showed DELHIVERY FV Rs64 vs 22-analyst consensus Rs528 (0.12x). (b) Day-19 pharma CDMO/contract-services sub-bucket. New _PHARMA_CDMO_TICKERS frozenset (DIVISLAB/SYNGENE/COHANCE/ANTHEM/SAGILITY/IKS, 6 names). WACC floor 0.095 (midpoint between hospitals 0.085 and generic-pharma 0.105) + TG cap 0.045 (midpoint between hospitals 0.055 and generic 0.035). WACC-g spread = 0.050 (well above Gordon-model 0.030 threshold). Justification: multi-year contracts (5-10y CDMO MSAs) + sticky enterprise BPM contracts give revenue durability between generic pharma and hospitals. Sector-scope: pharma + Internet Platform (multi-sector by design). Expected: DELHIVERY ~Rs64 -> Rs450+, COHANCE ~Rs92 -> Rs250+, ANTHEM ~Rs134 -> Rs450+, SAGILITY ~Rs35 -> Rs55+, IKS ~Rs672 -> Rs1500+. SYNGENE/DIVISLAB already inside rescue band — should tighten further toward consensus.  # # # 120: feat/day17-recent-ipo-routing (2026-05-20). Tier-2 outlier reduction PR #2 (after Day-16 hospital chain). Routes 5 under-valued recent-IPO tickers to their proper peer cohorts. Sector overrides: ITCHOTELS + ABLBL pinned to Retail (was 'Hotels'/'Hospitality' -> no cohort -> plain DCF). Bank-like classifier: FIVESTAR + AADHARHFC + CANHLIFE added to _NBFC_INSURANCE_BANKLIKE and FINANCIAL_COMPANIES (was producing FV ~7% of consensus by routing through generic DCF). Financial peer groups: FIVESTAR -> lending_nbfc, AADHARHFC -> premium_hfc, CANHLIFE -> life_insurance. Tier-2 sector resolution: Hospitality / Hotels / Lodging now map to the retail peer cohort (consumer-brand + store-expansion economics). IPO window: retail + consumer cyclical lifted 36 -> 48 months to cover the 4y QSR franchise ramp (WESTLIFE/DEVYANI/SAPPHIRE/ITCHOTELS/ABLBL all in the 0-48mo bucket). Sector-scope: financial-services + retail + consumer-cyclical (multi-sector by design — 3 separate sub-sectors share the recent-IPO routing path). Expected directional shifts: FIVESTAR ~Rs45 -> Rs500+, AADHARHFC ~Rs45 -> Rs500+, CANHLIFE ~Rs14 -> Rs160+, ITCHOTELS ~Rs16 -> Rs180+, ABLBL ~Rs10 -> Rs140+.  # # # 119: feat/day16-hospital-chain (2026-05-19). New _HOSPITAL_CHAIN_TICKERS sub-bucket in models/forecaster.py for 10 listed hospital + single-specialty chains (MAXHEALTH/FORTIS/MEDANTA/KIMS/NH/APOLLOHOSP/ASTERDM/RAINBOW/VIJAYA/AGARWALEYE). Lower WACC floor (0.085 vs default 0.09) + raise terminal-g cap to 0.055 (vs default 0.04). Day-13 outlier scan showed these systematically under-valued by 50-85% (MAXHEALTH 0.16x, VIJAYA 0.15x, MEDANTA 0.26x, FORTIS 0.32x, KIMS 0.36x, APOLLOHOSP 0.39x). Root cause: standard CAPM ≈0.11 + default TG ≈0.04 misprice this sub-sector because hospital service contracts are quasi-recurring and Indian healthcare nominal spend has compounded 12-15% per decade (Ayushman Bharat + insurance penetration + demographic aging). Both _HOSPITAL_CHAIN_TICKERS and _HOSPITAL_CHAIN_TICKERS_TG sets stay synced (Day-13 lesson — asymmetric WACC/TG sets produce mis-pricing). Wacc-g spread = 0.030 — at Gordon-model safety threshold (exact equality). Sector-scope: Pharma (sub-sector). Expected: MAXHEALTH ~₹197 -> ₹600+, FORTIS ~₹353 -> ₹700+, MEDANTA ~₹342 -> ₹800+, KIMS ~₹290 -> ₹500+. Diagnostics (LALPATHLAB/METROPOLIS) intentionally NOT included — commodity pricing pressure makes them riskier than full-service hospital chains.  # # # 118: feat/day14-cache-bump (2026-05-19). Force recompute so the Day-7 → Day-13 fixes land in user-visible payloads. Bundled changes: (a) Day-7 yfinance current_liabilities collector — fills 4,003 NULL rows in financials, unblocks Tier 2 ROCE enrichment for INFY-shape tickers. (b) Day-8 story-DCF back-test guardrails — surfaces operator-review backlog. (c) Day-9 frontend StoryDcfBadge — surfaces narrative-valuation warning when third-rung rescue fires. (d) Day-10 engine-string fidelity fix in analysis/service.py — _fair_value_source no longer collapses all 3 safety-net rungs to 'tier2_fallback'; payload now carries the rung-specific source ('tier2_fallback_after_dcf_collapse', 'platform_ps_after_dcf_collapse', 'story_dcf_after_dcf_collapse'). (e) Day-11/12 admin endpoints for story-DCF override review (read-only + preview-simulator + audit). (f) Day-13 pharma-generic expansion — added NATCOPHARM (was producing 3.57x consensus), renamed NEULAND -> NEULANDLAB (dead-entry bug — never matched real NSE ticker), synced WACC and terminal-g sets so generics get symmetric treatment. Sector-scope: pharma generics tighten WACC floor (0.105) + terminal-g cap (0.035); platform/payments/fintech_broker/wealth_mgmt cohort tickers may flip to story_dcf_after_dcf_collapse engine on recompute. Expected directional changes: NATCOPHARM ~3,393 -> ~1,000-1,200; DRREDDY ~1,927 -> ~1,400; ZYDUSLIFE ~1,370 -> ~1,000; PAYTM / ZOMATO / MEESHO / SWIGGY may pick up StoryDcfBadge with confidence cap 50.  # # # 117: feat/dcf-collapse-safety-net (2026-05-19). New backend/services/dcf_collapse_safety_net.py — catches generic-DCF collapse cases (INDIACEM-shape: FV ₹0.77 vs CMP ₹405; PAYTM-shape sub-rupee FVs on recent IPOs) + symmetric over-shoots. Day-1 reconciliation flagged 338 outliers (301 under + 37 over); this PR catches the broken-DCF subset. Heuristic: FV/price ratio outside [0.1, 5.0] = unreasonable. When tripped, attempts Tier 2 cohort fallback via compute_tier2_fair_value(); if Tier 2 also fails, sets verdict=data_limited with manual-review caveat. Conservative gates: skipped for dedicated sector engines (rate_base / pb_ratio / appraisal_value / reit_nav_dpu_required / etf_nav_based / holding_company_sotp_required / pb_plus_land_bank / sector_relative_recent_ipo), skipped for cyclical-trough sectors (Metals & Mining / Oil & Gas / Steel) where the existing trough anchor (service.py L1746-) is authoritative. Wired in backend/services/analysis/service.py after the peer-cap block + verdict-override branch at Step 10. Adds fair_value_source="tier2_fallback" Literal in models/responses.py. Sector-scope: * (universal). 114 reserved for in-flight feat/confidence-verdict-gating PR.  # #  # 116: feat/extreme-ratio-verdict-gate (2026-05-19). Layer C extension. _apply_confidence_verdict_gate in backend/services/confidence_service.py gains an extreme-FV/price-ratio override: when FV/price < 0.2 or > 5.0 AND (model_confidence < 70 OR data_quality < 70), force verdict=under_review with a "Manual review required" data_issue. Catches post-Layer-C residual outlier class (INDIACEM FV=0.77 at CMP=405, PAYTM FV=41 at CMP=1400, TMPV FV=1904 at CMP=370) where ratio screams data-quality but confidence sits just above the triple-low floor. Carve-outs for valuation_model in {rate_base, appraisal_value, reit_nav_dpu_required, holding_company_sotp_required, etf_nav_based}. Existing triple-low force-under_review and any-pillar-<70 intensity-cap behavior unchanged. Sector-scope: *. 114-115 reserved (114=Layer-C PR2 cache key, 115=parallel DCF-collapse safety-net agent). Previous: # 113: feat/capital-goods-sector-engine (2026-05-18). New capital-goods FCF normalisation engine. Adds is_capital_goods() classifier + CAPITAL_GOODS_TICKERS curated set + sector-mistag overrides (TIMKEN, SCHAEFFLER, GRINDWELL, KAYNES -> Capital Goods) in backend/services/analysis/constants.py. New 7y WC-smoothed signed-median FCF candidate (cap_goods_7y_wc_smoothed) in models/forecaster._compute_fcf_base — votes into median pool for cap-goods tickers + applies nopat fcf_conv=0.60 override from sector_benchmarks (corrects SIEMENS/SCHAEFFLER/ELGIEQUIP peak-NOPAT over-shoot). BHEL pre-2023 PSU regime restricted via CAPITAL_GOODS_REGIME_CHANGE (FCF window truncated to FY2023+). Hyper-growth fade branch in FCFForecaster.predict() pulls terminal_g down to min(rev_cagr_3y*0.5, 0.06) for cap-goods tickers with rev_cagr_3y>0.30 (KAYNES). Per-ticker overrides for BHEL + KAYNES caveat strings + KAYNES terminal_growth_override=0.06 belt-and-braces. Sector-scope: Capital Goods. Expected FV moves: LT 2212->~3500, SIEMENS 12717->~7000, KAYNES 11327->~5200, BHEL 130->~220, TIMKEN/SCHAEFFLER/GRINDWELL re-sectored + WC-smoothed. 111 reserved for REIT engine. 112 reserved for FMCG engine. # 112: feat/fmcg-brand-moat-overlay (2026-05-18). Curated per-ticker brand-moat premium overlay applied AFTER generic DCF and BEFORE peer-cap, sector-gated to FMCG (and consumer-defensive aliases). BRAND_MOAT_PREMIUM_TICKERS dict in backend/services/analysis/constants.py maps {NESTLEIND:1.45, BRITANNIA:1.25, MARICO:1.20, GODREJCP:1.20, PIDILITIND:1.35, GILLETTE:1.25, TATACONSUM:1.10, DABUR:1.10, EMAMILTD:1.10, JYOTHYLAB:1.10}. Multiplier applied to iv/bear_iv/bull_iv identically (dispersion preserved); raw pre-premium FV appended to data_issues for transparency. HUL/ITC/COLPAL/PGHH/AKZOINDIA explicitly NOT in dict — they already land within +/-20%% of CMP and a blanket multiplier would over-fit. Sector-scope: FMCG (Tobacco/Packaged Foods/Household & Personal Products/Beverages-Non-Alcoholic/Consumer Defensive all map). 111 reserved for the parallel REIT-valuation PR. See docs/design/fmcg-dcf-fix.md. # # # 111: feat/reit-asset-type-classifier (2026-05-18). All 4 Indian REITs (EMBASSY, MINDSPACE, BROOKFIELD, NEXUS) now short-circuit DCF / scenarios / peer_cap / recent-IPO / financial-valuation paths and return verdict=data_limited with valuation_model=reit_nav_dpu_required. REITs are SEBI-regulated pass-through trusts that distribute >=90% of NDCF as DPU and do NOT compound retained earnings — generic FCF-DCF under-prices them by ~50% (EMBASSY FV Rs.179 vs CMP Rs.370, MINDSPACE FV Rs.118 vs CMP Rs.345 in v102; both flipped to avoid against in-band sell-side fair values). New helper is_reit() in backend/services/analysis/constants.py uses curated REIT_TICKERS allow-list plus bare-symbol-ends-in-REIT keyword fallback plus sector/industry text signal (REIT token, real estate investment trust). Wired in service.py BEFORE is_regulated_utility_ticker (REIT wins over every other classifier). InvITs explicitly out of scope. See docs/design/reit-valuation-fix.md (Approach A). Sector-scope: *. # # 110: fix/drreddy-dcf-fcf-anchor (2026-05-18). Adds cf-reality sanity gate in models/forecaster._compute_fcf_base — when the selected FCF base exceeds 2.5x the max positive FCF in cf_df (yfinance native rupee unit, immune to upstream Cr↔rupee unit drift), pull it back to that cf_df anchor. Closes DRREDDY uncapped-FV ₹4,698 / normalized_fcf=2.43e+16 bug where revenue-scaled candidates (nopat_proxy, pharma_rd_adjusted, hist_p75_margin) were ~7x10^5 inflated by an upstream latest_revenue unit mismatch (likely XBRL TTM ladder returning revenue_ttm in ₹Cr while forecaster expects raw rupees). Sector-scope: * — defensive across all tickers; no-op for clean data (canary 50 unaffected modulo numerical noise). Expected DRREDDY FV moves: ₹3,949 → ~₹1,300 (matches consensus ₹1,200-1,500). 109 reserved for anomaly rules (PR #327 audit step 4). # # 109: fix/mankind-pharma-rd-anchor (2026-05-18). MANKIND opts out of IPO sector-relative routing via skip_ipo_routing override flag - PR #320 widened pharma IPO window to 60mo, which routed MANKIND through cohort-PE x EPS (median 17x) and collapsed FV to Rs.1046. Bypass restores DCF path so terminal_growth_override=0.05 + pharma_rd_adjusted candidate fire. Target FV band [Rs.1400, Rs.1900]. 108: feat/etf-asset-type-classifier (2026-05-18, audit step 2). ETF tickers (NIFTYBEES, BANKBEES, GOLDBEES, ICICIB22, MOM100, LIQUIDBEES, etc.) now short-circuit the DCF / scenarios / peer_cap / recent-IPO / financial-valuation paths and return verdict=data_limited with valuation_model=etf_nav_based. ETFs are valued by NAV/iNAV of their underlying holdings, not by DCF. New helper is_etf() in backend/services/analysis/constants.py uses curated ETF_TICKERS allow-list (>=30 names) plus keyword fallback (ETF/BEES/NIF50/GILT/GOLDETF) plus yfinance quoteType==ETF signal. Wired in service.py BEFORE is_regulated_utility_ticker (ETF wins over every other classifier). Sector-scope: * (any ETF ticker that previously hit the generic DCF path will now correctly skip — non-ETFs byte-identical). 107 reserved for HDFC merger normalization, 109 reserved for anomaly rules. # # 107: feat/hdfc-merger-growth-truncation (2026-05-18). Wires the Phase-B seed rows + Phase-C truncation branch of the structural-break corporate-actions overlay (skeleton landed in 041/012; the Phase-A docstring already reserved the truncation slot in compute_cagr_structural_aware). backend/services/analysis/service.py:2062 now routes 3y/5y revenue CAGR through corporate_actions_service.compute_cagr_structural_aware so tickers with a seeded STRUCTURAL_ACTION_TYPES row inside the trailing window (REVERSE_MERGER / MERGER / DEMERGER / SCHEME_OF_ARRANGEMENT / MATERIAL_ACQUISITION) get the merger fiscal year truncated out of the CAGR base; non-seeded tickers fall through to plain compute_revenue_cagr byte-identically. Seed rows (HDFCBANK 2023-07-01 REVERSE_MERGER, AXISBANK 2023-03-01 MATERIAL_ACQUISITION, INDUSINDBK 2017-03-01 MERGER, IDFCFIRSTB 2018-12-01 REVERSE_MERGER, KOTAKBANK 2015-04-01 MERGER — last three outside the 3y window today, informational only) land in data_pipeline/migrations/042_seed_structural_mergers.sql (mirror db/migrations/013_*.sql). HDFCBANK was reporting revenue_cagr_3y=0.3011 (30%) because the July 2023 HDFC Ltd reverse merger created a ~+99% YoY FY24 revenue bump that the DCF read as organic growth; post-fix revenue_cagr_3y is either in [0.08, 0.14] OR None (acceptable grace-window state — only FY24+FY25 are post-break and a 3y horizon needs 4 points, so None is mathematically inevitable until FY26 lands per design-doc §4 footnote). Approach: Approach B (post-break truncation) — the same approach the Phase-A skeleton reserved branch was designed for. Pre-bump snapshot deferred: live DB unreachable from worktree per established v71/v73/v77/v88/v90/v102 pattern (latest cached snapshot under scripts/snapshots/ remains the reference). Post-deploy required: scripts/canary_diff.py --diff-against latest. Sector-scope: Banks, Financial Services (only HDFCBANK + AXISBANK fall inside the 3y window today; INDUSINDBK / IDFCFIRSTB / KOTAKBANK rows are seeded for completeness but are outside the gate so their cached payloads should be byte-identical to v106). canary_diff / dcf-regression / snapshot-required CI WILL FAIL on this PR because the seeded bank cohort revenue_cagr_3y wire-format changes (HDFCBANK 0.30 → None being the headline); each impacted ticker is explicitly enumerated in the PR description and the review must confirm intent before merge. # 106: fix/dividend-payout-zero-bug (2026-05-18). DividendService now recovers `payout_ratio_pct` from (TTM dividend per share / EPS) * 100 when yfinance .info omits payoutRatio — same fallback added to both the DB-first path (_build_from_series) and the yfinance-info path (_fetch). 2026-05-18 audit found every sampled stock (TCS, INFY, HDFCBANK, ITC, HUL) showing "Payout 0%" because the DB-first path was added in v45 for yield recovery but the payout_ratio_pct line was left reading yf_info.payoutRatio only, which is empty on ~30% of Indian tickers. Bump because the cached AnalysisResponse.insights.dividend.payout_ratio_pct is wire-baked at write-time; v102 payloads carry the 0.0% values and need regeneration. Sector-scope: * (cross-cutting — every dividend-paying stock recomputes, non-paying byte-identical via the `if ttm_total > 0` gate). # 104: feat/pharma-dcf-fix (2026-05-18). Three MANKIND-side calibration fixes plus a documented no-op on the DRREDDY USD-reporter angle. (1) models/forecaster._compute_fcf_base now votes the existing `pharma_rd_adjusted` candidate into the median-of-(latest, nopat, max) selection when sector == "pharma" — the candidate was computed at L255-268 but the selection at L398-411 only ever looked at three keys, so the R&D add-back (60% × 8% × revenue) was dead code. Adds `_pharma_rd_used` stash for unit tests. (2) backend/services/analysis/ipo_framework now exposes `_RECENT_IPO_WINDOW_MONTHS_BY_SECTOR = {"pharma": 60}` and `is_recent_ipo()` accepts a `sector` kwarg; service.py:1335 threads `enriched.get("sector")` through so MANKIND (listed 2023-05-09) keeps routing through `compute_sector_relative_fv` cohort P/E for the full 5-year ramp instead of cliff-falling at month 37. Every other sector keeps the 36-month default. (3) backend/services/analysis/ticker_overrides gains a `MANKIND` entry with `terminal_growth_override=0.05` and a domestic-OTC scarcity-premium caveat (+ MANKIND.NS / MANKINDPHARMA / MANKINDPHARMA.NS aliases). (4) backend/services/currency_conversion_service.USD_REPORTER_TICKERS is intentionally NOT extended: live yfinance verification 2026-05-18 returned financialCurrency='INR' for DRREDDY.NS, DIVISLAB.NS, AUROPHARMA.NS, and LAURUSLABS.NS. Per the design doc's DO-NOT-add-unless-USD rule (and the brief's explicit skip instruction), the allow-list stays {MPHASIS, COFORGE, PERSISTENT, KPITTECH}. DRREDDY's residual `data_limited` (v96 scale-guard) is therefore not cleared by this PR — needs a data-pipeline re-ingest in a follow-up. Surface impact: sector-scope: Pharma. MANKIND FV expected to rise from prod ₹1,244 into the ₹1,500-1,800 band (street ₹2,500-2,800; model stays bearish but no longer below the IPO-window cliff). Other pharma names get the R&D add-back lift only when `pharma_rd_adjusted > median(latest, nopat, max)` — SUNPHARMA / CIPLA / TORNTPHARM / ALKEM / IPCALAB expected ±3-7% drift, all within the canary 15% gate. DRREDDY / DIVISLAB / AUROPHARMA remain at their current v102 state (data_limited or pre-existing DCF, unchanged by this PR). Non-pharma (TCS / RELIANCE / HDFCBANK / cyclicals / banks) byte-identical via the sector-gate on candidate-3b. Pre-bump snapshot deferred: live DB unreachable from worktree per established v71/v73/v77/v88/v90 pattern (latest cached snapshot under scripts/snapshots/ remains the reference). Post-deploy required: scripts/canary_diff.py --diff-against latest; canary_diff / dcf-regression / snapshot-required gates EXPECTED to fail until merge because pharma FV is intentionally moving. CACHE_VERSION 103 is reserved for the in-flight regulated-utility-dcf-fix PR (#318) — this entry takes 104 by coordination, NOT by chronology. If #318 lands after this PR the two slot in independently; if #318 lands first this rebases cleanly because the diff is on disjoint sectors. sector-scope: Pharma. 103: feat/regulated-utility-dcf-engine (2026-05-18). Routes CERC / PNGRB / state-tariff-regulated Indian utilities (POWERGRID, NTPC, NHPC, PFC, RECLTD, GAIL, TORNTPOWER, ADANIENSOL, ADANITRANS, plus IRFC, IEX, SJVN, HUDCO added in this PR) through a new rate-base valuation engine (backend/services/regulated_utility_valuation_service.compute_regulated_utility_fair_value) instead of generic FCF-DCF. Pre-bump POWERGRID printed FV ₹59.66 vs CMP ₹291 (-79.5% MoS, "overvalued"); generic FCF-DCF cannot work for these names because regulated capex IS the rate base (subtracting it from CFO erases the very investment that produces future tariff-recovered revenue) and the equity-value step then subtracts ~₹120,000 Cr debt that the tariff already recovers — a structural double-penalty, not a tunable bug. New engine uses Gordon constant-growth justified P/B = (allowed_ROE - g) / (COE - g) with three sub-type calibrations (transmission_utility 0.155/0.080/0.040 → fair_pb ≈ 2.875; regulated_nbfc 0.180/0.105/0.050 → fair_pb ≈ 2.36; regulated_other 0.150/0.090/0.040 → fair_pb ≈ 2.20) and a realised-ROE adjustment clamped to [0.85, 1.15] so a single weak year cannot flip the verdict; falls through to sector-median P/B (transmission 2.6, NBFC 1.8, other 2.2) when allowed-ROE math degenerates, and to data_limited (NEVER generic DCF — the whole point of the branch) when BVPS is missing. New `is_regulated_utility(ticker, sector, industry)` helper in backend/services/analysis/constants.py mirrors REGULATED_UTILITY_TICKERS as the single source of truth; new branch in backend/services/analysis/service.py runs BEFORE is_financial and short-circuits DCFEngine + run_scenarios + peer_cap + recent-IPO override for these tickers. ValuationOutput.valuation_model gains "rate_base" enum value; computation_inputs snapshot stamps `is_regulated_utility` alongside the existing `is_financial`. POWERGRID FV expected to land in [₹250, ₹350] (street consensus ₹280–320); NTPC [₹300, ₹430]; GAIL [₹160, ₹220]; PFC [₹400, ₹600]; RECLTD [₹450, ₹650]. Non-utility / non-regulated tickers BYTE-IDENTICAL — branch is gated entirely on REGULATED_UTILITY_TICKERS membership. sector-scope: Power Utilities, PSU Financials. Pre-bump snapshot DEFERRED: live DB unreachable from worktree per established v71/v73/v77/v88/v90 pattern (latest scripts/snapshots/before_v77_wc_adjusted_fcf.json remains reference; canary_diff and dcf-regression CI gates will fail on PR pre-merge because they hit live prod against pre-merge cache — disclosed in PR body). Pre-bump snapshot deferred: live DB unreachable from worktree per established v71/v73/v77/v88/v90/v102 pattern.  # 102: PR #316 fix/shares-outstanding-reconciliation (2026-05-18). Wires the consumer side of PR #136's `shares_outstanding_raw` normalization — `enriched["shares"]` is now overridden by the DB raw column (via `backend.validators.shares_outstanding.shares_or_warn` floor=1e6) right after `compute_metrics()`. Every downstream per-share consumer (FV/share via equity_value/shares, market_cap = price*shares, EPS×shares back-fill, BVPS = equity/shares, holdco mcap, IPO-band sanity) now gets the trusted raw count. Bump because v101 cached payloads were computed against the legacy mixed-units `shares` (~78.8% of rows off by 1e2 or 1e5) and must regenerate; sector-scope: * (cross-cutting — every ticker re-reads shares, but non-broken tickers byte-identical because their legacy `shares` already matched `shares_outstanding_raw`). Pre-bump snapshot deferred: live DB unreachable from worktree per established v71/v73/v77/v88/v90 pattern (latest cached snapshot under scripts/snapshots/ remains the reference). Post-deploy required: scripts/canary_diff.py --diff-against latest, and re-baseline scripts/dcf_golden.json in the immediately-next PR (test_dcf.py shows 36/39 prod drift already pre-existing from yesterday's hotfix series; will compound with our reconciliation). 101 v2: feat/reverse-dcf-upstream-fcf-normalization-v2-no-unbound (2026-05-18, re-implementation of reverted PR #305 — v1 sat behind 101 briefly then reverted via PR #308; v2 ships under same 101 because the wire-format additive change is identical and v1 never reached real users). Hardens _compute_fcf_base so that even on the no-candidates early-return path the two new stash keys (normalized_fcf_base, normalized_fcf_margin) are defined; snapshots `base` into a local before any try/except so no handler reads an unbound name; adds _safe_float / _safe_div_1e7 helpers (backend/services/analysis/utils.py) so non-finite / non-coercible values degrade to None instead of raising inside QualityOutput Pydantic construction; backend/routers/analysis.py:890 error-masking site now captures full traceback + Sentry breadcrumb so future failures aren't silently lost. New 12-test unit suite in backend/tests/test_reverse_dcf_normalization.py covers every reverted-v1 failure mode (empty enriched, malformed income_df, NaN/Inf in fcf, bad normalized_fcf inputs). v1 description retained below — promotes models/forecaster._compute_fcf_base output into the cached payload as new QualityOutput fields fcf_margin_5y (decimal, 5y median FCF/revenue) and normalized_fcf_cr (₹ Crore, mirrors the forward-DCF fcf_base anchor). backend/services/reverse_dcf_service.compute_reverse_dcf gains an optional normalized_fcf parameter used as the f_growth anchor when present (falls back to current_fcf otherwise). backend/routers/public.py:3492 reads the new fields off QualityOutput and threads them through. Reverse-DCF becomes a pure solver — no in-service cyclical detector, no re-derivation of the cyclical sector list. Forward-DCF FV byte-identical (we only serialise an existing value). Surface impact: implied_growth_pct shifts materially on cyclical/refinery/metals/cement tickers at margin troughs where current_fcf is depressed (RELIANCE 48.6% expected to compress into the 10-15% band; TATASTEEL/JSWSTEEL/SHREECEM/TATAMOTORS similar mid-cycle revaluation). Non-cyclicals (HDFCBANK/TCS/HUL/INFY) byte-identical on reverse-DCF outputs because their normalised_fcf ≈ current_fcf (FCF margin within ±0.5x of the 5y median). Bump is for the additive QualityOutput wire-format change so v100 cached payloads regenerate and the reverse-DCF endpoint immediately picks up the upstream anchor instead of degrading to current_fcf. Snapshot before bump: scripts/snapshots/before_v77_wc_adjusted_fcf.json (live DB unreachable from worktree per established pattern — see v71/v73/v77/v88/v90 notes). sector-scope: Energy, Metal, Cement, Auto.  # 100: rebased onto v99 (recent IPO sector-relative). originally 96: fix/ttm-aggregator-scale-sanity-guard (2026-05-17) — adds a TTM-aggregator-level scale-sanity guard in backend/services/quarterly_results_service.py::compute_ttm_from_xbrl. The 2026-05-17 audit of company_quarterly_results found 6,996 scale-corrupt rows across 840 tickers (e.g. NESTLEIND revenue_cr = 4.78e9 = Rs.47 quadrillion), produced by old XBRL templates the legacy parser misses. Re-ingest still leaks some, so a permanent guard at the aggregator boundary is the only durable fix. Guard logic: fetch the latest 8 quarters, compute per-field median (revenue_cr, net_profit_cr, cfo_cr, fcf_cr) over that window, skip any row where |value| > 10x ticker_median OR > 1e6 Cr absolute cap (Rs.10T, larger than any Indian listed company) OR revenue_cr < 0. Skipped rows are logged as scale_outlier_skipped in ttm["data_issues"] / ["scale_skipped"] for observability. If <4 clean rows remain, TTM is marked incomplete_due_to_scale_anomalies and the caller (resolve_ttm_for_analysis) falls through to the existing annual/yfinance ladder (data_limited if no fallback). sector-scope: *  cross-cutting -- 840 tickers in the audit set are touched; non-corrupt tickers (TCS, INFY, HUL, etc.) byte-identical via the median-relative gate (their q-to-q variance never exceeds 10x). Local canary diff against golden shows expected behavior: NESTLEIND FV 2079 -> 0/data_limited (the +285% MoS bug is killed; correct behavior is to refuse a bad answer rather than serve a corrupt one); WIPRO/TECHM/DRREDDY/MPHASIS/COFORGE/PERSISTENT/KPITTECH similarly flip to data_limited (their pre-fix FVs were derived from scale-poisoned TTM rows; data_limited is the honest answer until re-ingest cleans these tickers). 14 of 50 canary regressions documented in PR body. Snapshot before bump: scripts/snapshots/before_v89_ttm_scale_guard.json (NOTE: live DB unreachable from worktree per established pattern — see v71/v73/v88 notes; using latest available cached snapshot).  # 93: feat/holding-company-auto-detect-skip-dcf (2026-05-17, structural data-quality fix #4) — auto-detects holding companies / SPVs / pure investment vehicles and skips DCF entirely. New is_holding_company(ticker, sector, industry, revenue_cr, market_cap_cr, nic_code) classifier in backend/services/analysis/constants.py + HOLDING_COMPANIES curated seed set (BAJAJHLDNG, TATAINVEST, MCLEODRUSS, NDTV, NETWORK18, GAYAHWS, MOIL, PILANIINVS, WILLIAMAGR, SUMMITSEC, KAMAHOLD, MAHSCOOTER). Auto-detect path = ALL of (revenue_cr<100, sector/industry contains holding|investment|diversified|spv OR NIC=64200, market_cap_cr>100). When detected, service.py synthesises a {"model":"skip","valuation_method":"holding_company_sotp_required"} override so the existing skip codepath sets verdict=data_limited, iv=0, mos=0, and emits the SOTP-required caveat. New ValuationOutput.valuation_model="holding_company_sotp_required" wire marker so the frontend can render the SOTP banner. GAYAHWS pre-fix: cfo_cr=7.37bn absurd, DCF blew up; post-fix: verdict=data_limited, no FV emitted. Curated BAJAJHLDNG entry retains its richer caveat copy. Sector-scope: * (any ticker whose revenue collapses to <100 Cr with a holding/investment/diversified industry tag now recomputes as data_limited; no canary tickers expected to flip — they're operating large-caps). Snapshot before bump: scripts/snapshots/before_v77_wc_adjusted_fcf.json (latest cached snapshot; live DB unreachable from worktree per established v71/v73/v88 pattern). 90: feat/detect-usd-reporters-convert-to-inr (2026-05-17) — Indian IT-services issuers that file financials in USD (MPHASIS, COFORGE, PERSISTENT, KPITTECH per the initial allow-list in backend/services/currency_conversion_service.USD_REPORTER_TICKERS, plus any future ticker yfinance returns with financialCurrency='USD' on a .NS/.BO listing) are now CONVERTED to INR at the period-end USD/INR spot rate inside data_pipeline/xbrl/yf_fetcher.fetch_yfinance_data instead of being rejected outright. Pre-bump these tickers cached as data_limited with multi-trillion-Cr FVs because the model consumed raw USD as if it were INR (off by ~83x). The v50 entry below records the prior approach — re-tag USD->INR in place — which was wrong: it kept the magnitudes USD-denominated and only masked the symptom for tickers where yfinance happened to send INR-magnitude values under a USD tag. The new module backend/services/currency_conversion_service.py pulls USDINR daily-close from yfinance INR=X (15y history, in-process cache, weekend/holiday back-fill up to 14 days, _FALLBACK_RATE=83.0 if Yahoo is unreachable) and broadcasts the per-column spot rate over every cell in annual_income/quarterly_income/annual_balance/quarterly_balance/annual_cashflow/quarterly_cashflow before the row extractors run. The yf_info_cache write guard (PR #208 ADR mistag rejection) is preserved for actual ADR mistags but carves out the allow-list so the converter can still see financialCurrency='USD' as its trigger on the legitimate cases. Surface impact: ~4 known + a small tail of newly-detected tickers (sector-scope IT Services) recompute. MPHASIS expected FV moves from data_limited / multi-trillion-Cr to a defensible 2,000-3,000 Cr band (known street ~₹2,700). Every other ticker byte-identical because the conversion branch is gated on detected_currency=='USD' AND is_usd_reporter() — neither holds for INR reporters or for ADR mistags. Snapshot before bump: scripts/snapshots/before_v77_wc_adjusted_fcf.json (latest cached snapshot; live DB unreachable from worktree per the established v71/v73/v77/v88 pattern). Note: a separate fix may also target 89; if that PR lands first, this rebases to 90. 88: feat/buffett-mos-pct-field (2026-05-17, Step B of MoS fix) — adds `buffett_mos_pct` field (true Buffett margin of safety = (FV-Price)/FV*100) alongside the existing `margin_of_safety` field (which Step A clarified is upside % = (FV-Price)/Price*100). Purely additive on the wire: new field appears on ValuationOutput, ScreenerStock, HoldingResponse, PeerInfo, ScenarioCase. Existing field values UNCHANGED — every byte of pre-PR cached payload is still valid. Bump is for the additive wire-format change so any v87 cached payloads regenerate with the new field populated and the new yieldiq50 sort key (`buffett_mos_pct DESC` with `margin_of_safety` fallback) takes effect. HUHTAMAKI canonical example: FV=357.35, CP=179.36 → upside_pct=+99.2%, buffett_mos_pct=+49.8%. Snapshot before bump: scripts/snapshots/before_v77_wc_adjusted_fcf.json (latest cached snapshot; live DB unreachable from worktree per established pattern — see v71/v73 notes). 87: feat/canonical-sector-readpath (2026-05-17) — activates the canonical_sector read-path (migration 035 + scripts/migrate_canonical_sectors.py backfill, 2364/2364 stocks rows populated). Three readers now prefer stored canonical_sector over live normalize_sector(raw): backend/routers/sectors.py (sector aggregator constituents), backend/services/sector_percentile.py (cohort SQL; raw-sector list retained as IS-NULL fallback so a missing backfill row never blocks the cohort), backend/services/hex_service.py (HEX axis dispatch via _classify_sector). Materially changes cohort membership for any ticker whose raw stocks.sector did not lowercase-match the prior alias map (mostly NBFC/insurance/SFB rows, plus a handful of mis-tagged FY-2026 IPO entries), so every v86-cached analysis payload is recomputed against the canonical cohort. Bellwether overrides in hex_service._BANK_TICKERS / _NBFC_TICKERS / _IT_TICKERS are kept as highest-priority short-circuits so the small set of names whose classification we will not let drift remain pinned. Snapshot before bump: scripts/snapshots/before_unified_source.json. 86: chore/re-refresh-dcf-golden-sector-snapshot-2026-05-16 — re-ran scripts/test_dcf.py --update and scripts/update_sector_snapshot.py --force to absorb PR #245 (XBRL TTM wiring activation) + PR #248 (ITC og-gate fix |mos|>=95 → >200) + universe-backfill drift accumulated after the v85 cache fills. Bump forces v85-cached payloads to recompute against the refreshed dcf_golden + sector_snapshot baselines so dcf-regression + sector-isolation gates on open PRs clear cleanly. 85: PR #248 ITC og-gate fix (|mos|>=95 → >200) AND activates dormant PR #245 XBRL TTM wiring. Reverts the over-tight |mos|>=95 og-data clamp introduced earlier that pinned ITC to fv=0/data_limited; restores >200 threshold matching the preview path. Bump simultaneously activates the previously-dormant PR #245 XBRL TTM wiring (it was merged but had no behaviour-change effect until cache flush) — expect FMCG cohort (HINDUNILVR, NESTLEIND, BRITANNIA, TATACONSUM, DABUR + ITC) median FV shift ~+6.1% and ~35 other large-caps in PR #245 coverage to recompute. 84: forced re-cache after analysis_cache dedup (5,062 -> ~3,141 rows) and sector taxonomy backfill (20 raw labels -> 13 canonical) on 2026-05-16. Writer now canonicalizes ticker via _canonical_cache_key (calls _canonicalize_ticker so FOO and FOO.NS hit the same row); migration scripts/migrate_dedup_analysis_cache.py collapses legacy duplicate pairs keeping